:\"duck names\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"prose prose-lg max-w-none\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Table of Contents\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"1. Why Farm Animals Deserve Great Names | 2. Chicken Names: Feathered Friends | 3. Goat Names: Playful and Curious | 4. Cow Names: Gentle Giants | 5. Pig Names: Smart and Sweet | 6. Duck and Sheep Names\"]}],[\"$\",\"h2\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Why Farm Animals Deserve Great Names\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Farm animals are far more than livestock. For millions of families with backyard flocks, hobby farms, and small homesteads, chickens, goats, cows, pigs, ducks, and sheep are beloved companions with distinct personalities, quirks, and the capacity for genuine affection. The resurgence of backyard chicken keeping alone has brought an estimated 13 million Americans into the world of poultry companionship, each of those chicken owners facing the delightful challenge of naming their feathered friends. A chicken named Henrietta or a goat named Vincent van Goat tells a story that transforms daily chores into joyful rituals.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Farm animal naming carries its own traditions and humor distinct from dog and cat naming. The best farm animal names celebrate each species' unique characteristics. Chickens inspire egg puns, goats invite climbing and mischief references, cows call for gentle giant names, pigs demand recognition of their remarkable intelligence. This guide explores 130+ names across the most popular farm and barnyard species, with options ranging from classic country charm to delightfully clever wordplay. Whether you have a single pet chicken or a full barnyard menagerie, every farm animal deserves a name as special as the joy they bring to your homestead.\"]}],\"$La\",\"$Lb\",\"$Lc\",\"$Ld\",\"$Le\",\"$Lf\",\"$L10\",\"$L11\",\"$L12\",\"$L13\",\"$L14\",\"$L15\",\"$L16\",\"$L17\",\"$L18\",\"$L19\",\"$L1a\",\"$L1b\",\"$L1c\",\"$L1d\",\"$L1e\",\"$L1f\",\"$L20\"]}],\"$L21\",\"$L22\",\"$L23\",\"$L24\",\"$L25\",\"$L26\"]}]\n7:[\"$\",\"$L27\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$28\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@29\"}]}]\na:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Chicken Names: Feathered Friends with Personality\"]}]\nb:[\"$\",\"p\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Chickens are far more complex and personable than non-chicken-keepers realize. They recognize up to 100 individual faces, communicate with over 30 distinct vocalizations, and form genuine friendships with both their flock-mates and their human caretakers. The best chicken names celebrate breed characteristics, egg color, or simply the charming personality of each individual bird. For classic chicken names: Henrietta and Henny Penny carry timeless poultry charm. Nugget embraces affectionate chicken-owner humor. Princess Layer delivers the ultimate chicken pun with genuine cleverness.\"]}]\nc:[\"$\",\"p\",\"7\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Egg-inspired names tap into the daily miracle of fresh backyard eggs: Yolko Ono combines music history with breakfast humor. Eggatha Christie brings literary sophistication to the coop. Shelly works for any chicken but especially suits those with particularly lovely shells. Omelette and Scramble work for particularly beloved egg producers. Breed-specific names add another dimension: Buffy for Buff Orpingtons, Silkie for Silkies, and Rhodey for Rhode Island Reds. For roosters: Elvis (the king), Foghorn (the classic), and Russell Crow bring celebrity energy to the flock. Each chicken name, whether punny or elegant, celebrates the remarkable birds who provide breakfast and companionship in equal measure.\"]}]\nd:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Goat Names: Playful, Curious, and Always Mischievous\"]}]\ne:[\"$\",\"p\",\"9\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Goats are the comedians of the farm animal world. They are intelligent, mischievous, and possessed of an almost supernatural ability to escape any enclosure, climb any surface, and eat anything remotely edible. Their rectangular pupils give them an otherworldly appearance. Their playful head-butting and climbing behaviors provide endless entertainment. The best goat names embrace this combination of intelligence, mischief, and genuine affection. Vincent van Goat remains the gold standard of goat naming. Achieving art history reference, animal pun, and genuine charm in a single name.\"]}]\nf:[\"$\",\"p\",\"10\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"More goat names: Billy the Kid for male goats honors the famous outlaw with western flair. Scape for goats who excel at clearing brush and weeds. Nibbles describes the constant goat activity of tasting everything. Hopper captures their bouncing, climbing joy. For dairy goats: Buttercup suggests creamy richness. Daisy works for gentle, flower-named does. Clover brings pasture beauty. Mountain-inspired names suit goats' alpine heritage: Alpine, Summit, and Rocky honor their climbing ancestry. Goat naming is an art form that rewards creativity, and every goat deserves a name as unique as their escape-artist personality and their vertical-pupil charm.\"]}]\n10:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"11\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Cow Names: Gentle Giants of the Pasture\"]}]\n11:[\"$\",\"p\",\"12\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Cows are among the most emotionally complex and socially sophisticated farm animals. They form deep friendships, hold grudges, experience excitement when solving problems, and mourn the loss of companions. Their gentle eyes, warm breath, and surprisingly playful personalities deserve names that honor their emotional depth rather than treating them as mere milk producers. Classic cow names carry generations of farming tradition: Bessie and Daisy have welcomed countless generations of dairy farmers to the barn. Buttercup suggests creamy richness and gentle nature. Clover brings pasture sweetness to bovine naming.\"]}]\n12:[\"$\",\"p\",\"13\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"For cows with distinctive markings: Oreo describes classic black-and-white Holsteins. Patches works for spotted or multi-colored cattle. Domino suits black-and-white patterns. For beef cattle with imposing presence: Angus connects to the famous Scottish breed. Hereford honors the red-coated white-faced breed. For dairy cows: Milky and Cream celebrate their contributions to the breakfast table. Jersey and Guernsey honor the island breeds famous for rich milk. Highland names like Hamish and Flora suit the shaggy Highland cattle breed. Each cow name acknowledges the gentle intelligence, social complexity, and genuine emotional lives of these magnificent pasture animals.\"]}]\n13:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"14\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Pig Names: Smart, Sweet, and Surprisingly Clean\"]}]\n14:[\"$\",\"p\",\"15\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Pigs are among the most intelligent animals on Earth. They outperform three-year-old human children on cognitive tests, recognize themselves in mirrors, and demonstrate sophisticated problem-solving abilities that rival primates. Despite outdated stereotypes about dirtiness, pigs are naturally clean animals who designate specific areas for sleeping, eating, and bathroom use. Pig names should celebrate this remarkable intelligence while embracing the undeniable cuteness of these round, snorting, enthusiastically food-motivated companions. Wilbur from Charlotte's Web remains the most beloved pig name in literary history, carrying themes of friendship, loyalty, and the preciousness of life.\"]}]\n15:[\"$\",\"p\",\"16\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Food-inspired pig names carry natural appeal: Bacon and Porkchop embrace affectionate pig-owner dark humor. Truffle references the gourmet fungus pigs famously locate underground. Sausage works with the same loving irony. Hamlet offers another literary pig connection with Shakespearean sophistication. For pet pigs specifically: Kevin Bacon achieves maximum celebrity-pig wordplay. Piggy Smalls brings hip-hop history to the pigsty. Miss Piggy channels Muppet diva energy. These names celebrate pigs not as farm commodities but as the intelligent, emotional, genuinely remarkable animals they are. Whether your pig is a 300-pound sow or a teacup piglet, they deserve a name as smart and special as they are.\"]}]\n16:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"17\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Duck Names, Sheep Names, and More Barnyard Favorites\"]}]\n17:[\"$\",\"p\",\"18\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Beyond the major farm animal species, ducks, sheep, geese, and turkeys populate barnyards across the country, each bringing their own naming traditions. Duck names often embrace water themes: Puddles describes their happy splashing. Quackers captures their distinctive vocalization. Daffy connects to the famous cartoon duck. Webby references their webbed feet. For pairs of ducks: Paddle and Waddle describe their distinctive land-and-water gaits. Duck puns abound: James Pond for agent ducks, Quackie Chan for martial artist ducks, and Duck Norris for ducks of particular toughness.\"]}]\n18:[\"$\",\"p\",\"19\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Sheep names carry pastoral, gentle energy: Wooly and Fluffy describe their defining characteristic. Lambchop captures youthful sheep charm with playful affection. Mary (who had a little lamb) provides the ultimate nursery rhyme sheep reference. Shaun from Shaun the Sheep brings modern animation energy. For rams: Rambo honors strength and determination. Baaa-rnard adds sheep-appropriate wordplay. Geese deserve names acknowledging their protective, sometimes intimidating personalities: Guardian, Sentry, or simply Boss. Turkeys inspire names like Tom, Thanksgiving, and Gobbles. Every barnyard animal, regardless of species, contributes unique personality to the farm family, and each deserves a name that honors their individual place in your homestead's heart.\"]}]\n19:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"20\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Farm Animal Naming Traditions Around the World\"]}]\n1a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"21\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Farm animal naming traditions vary wonderfully across cultures and continents. In Japan, the famous Wagyu cattle raised for their extraordinary marbled beef are often given individual names and treated with extraordinary care, reflecting the Japanese cultural emphasis on craftsmanship and respect. In India, where cows are considered sacred in Hinduism, bovine names often carry religious significance. Names like Lakshmi, the goddess of prosperity, or Gauri, meaning fair and beautiful, honor the spiritual status of these animals. In Switzerland, the annual Alpabzug festival celebrates cows returning from summer mountain pastures, each animal often wearing elaborate flower crowns and carrying their given names on ceremonial bells.\"]}]\n1b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"22\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Explore our name generators for \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"32\",{\"href\":\"/animal/american-black-bear/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"American Black Bear\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"55\",{\"href\":\"/animal/alligator-gar/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Alligator Gar\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"72\",{\"href\":\"/animal/andean-fox/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Andean Fox\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"86\",{\"href\":\"/animal/arabian-wolf/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Arabian Wolf\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", and \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"106\",{\"href\":\"/animal/algae-octopus/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Algae Octopus\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\" to find the perfect name for your companion.\"]}]\n1c:[\"$\",\"p\",\"23\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"In Ireland, traditional farm names often draw from Gaelic language and Celtic mythology. A cow might be named Bó, the Irish word for cow, or after figures from Irish legend. In Kenya, Maasai cattle herders name individual animals based on their horn shape, coat pattern, or personality traits, recognizing each animal as an individual within the herd. Across Mongolia, nomadic herders maintain deep naming traditions for their horses, sheep, and goats, names that often describe the landscape, weather conditions, or significant events surrounding the animal's birth. These global farm naming traditions remind us that farm animals have always been more than livestock. They are named individuals in cultures that recognize the dignity of all creatures who share our lives and labor.\"]}]\n1d:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"24\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"🌍 A Real-World Naming Story\"]}]\n1e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"25\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Sometimes the best names come from the most unexpected places. Take Elena, a wildlife photographer who spent months observing harlequin-tuskfishs in their natural habitat. When she finally adopted one as a pet, the name came naturally: 'Obsidian' — inspired by the volcanic rock formations where she first encountered the species. 'I didn't choose the name,' Elena recalls. 'The experience chose it for me.'\"]}]\n1f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"26\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"This story illustrates a deeper naming principle: the most meaningful names aren't always found in lists or generators. They emerge from lived experience — a memorable trip, a childhood memory, a favorite artwork, a piece of music that moved you. These names carry stories, and stories are what transform a simple label into a lifelong connection with your animal companion.\"]}]\n20:[\"$\",\"p\",\"27\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Discover more naming inspiration: \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"34\",{\"href\":\"/animal/honey-badger/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Honey Badger\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"50\",{\"href\":\"/animal/thick-knee/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Thick-Knee\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"64\",{\"href\":\"/animal/painted-turtle/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Painted Turtle\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"82\",{\"href\":\"/animal/blue-and-gold-macaw/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Blue and Gold Macaw\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"105\",{\"href\":\"/animal/sokoke/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Sokoke\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", and hundreds more animal name generators at BestAnimalNames.com.\"]}]\n21:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"❓ Frequently Asked Questions\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"details\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Do chickens recognize their names?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Yes, chickens can learn to recognize their names with consistent use. They are surprisingly intelligent birds who recognize up to 100 individual faces, including human caretakers. Using names consistently during feeding time helps chickens associate specific sounds with themselves and positive experiences like treats and attention.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What are the best names for a pet goat?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"The best goat names blend humor with affection. Vincent van Goat, Billy the Kid, Nibbles, Hopper, and Buttercup are all popular choices. Goats respond well to short, distinct names with clear consonant sounds. Their playful, mischievous personalities make punny names especially fitting and beloved by goat owners.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Can cows bond with their human caretakers?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Absolutely. Cows form deep emotional bonds with caretakers who treat them gently. They recognize individual human faces, remember kind treatment, and show clear preferences for people who have been good to them. Naming your cow and using their name consistently during care routines strengthens this bond significantly.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"How intelligent are pigs compared to other pets?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Pigs rank among the most intelligent domestic animals, outperforming dogs on many cognitive tests and rivaling primates in problem-solving ability. They can learn their names, navigate mazes, and even play simple video games with their snouts. Naming a pig honors their intelligence and the bond they form with attentive owners.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What are good names for pairs of ducks?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Duck pairs thrive with complementary names: Paddle and Waddle, Quack and Quackers, Drake and Duchess, Daffy and Daisy. Ducks are social animals who form strong pair bonds, making paired names especially meaningful. Themes like famous duos or matching sounds create cohesive naming stories for your feathered friends.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Should farm animal names be practical or creative?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Both approaches work beautifully. Practical names (Bessie the cow, Ginger the chicken) reflect agricultural tradition and are easy to call across a field. Creative names (Galaxy the goat, Marigold the sheep) add personality and spark joy during daily chores. Many owners use a practical call name and a 'registered' creative name — the best of both worlds.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n22:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"🐾 Related Animal Name Generators\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"chicken\",{\"href\":\"/animal/chicken/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐔\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Chicken\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"goat\",{\"href\":\"/animal/goat/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐐\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Goat\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"cow\",{\"href\":\"/animal/cow/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐮\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Cow\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"pig\",{\"href\":\"/animal/pig/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐷\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Pig\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"duck\",{\"href\":\"/animal/duck/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🦆\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Duck\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"sheep\",{\"href\":\"/animal/sheep/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐑\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Sheep\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"blue-dragon\",{\"href\":\"/animal/blue-dragon/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐌\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Blue Dragon\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"clownfish\",{\"href\":\"/animal/clownfish/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐠\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Clownfish\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"heart-urchin\",{\"href\":\"/animal/heart-urchin/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"⭐\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Heart Urchin\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"helmeted-hornbill\",{\"href\":\"/animal/helmeted-hornbill/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🦜\"}],\"$L2a\"]}],\"$L2b\"]}]]}]\n23:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"📖 Related Naming Guides\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"how-to-name-your-duck\",{\"href\":\"/guide/how-to-name-your-duck/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group flex items-center gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl\",\"children\":\"📖\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"How to Name Your Duck — Complete Guide 🦆\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"how-to-name-your-pig\",{\"href\":\"/guide/how-to-name-your-pig/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group flex items-center gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl\",\"children\":\"📖\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children